province = 51
blurb = "This text explains the history of the Arimatsu tie-dyeing. It mentions that Arimatsu and Narumi (located in modern-day Nagoya) are the centers of this industry. It describes the intricate process of tying the cloth to create patterns like \"spider\" (kumo) and \"fawn spot\" (kanoko), and mentions the use of high-quality indigo dye."
